# The Haven's swap table (docs/ERRANDS.md, "Duties"; Missions/Errands/RZ_DutyHaven.c, SwapTable): the
# sixteen who come to the table, in their own words. Each stands a step behind the table while it's
# their turn (RZ_TalkDutyPerson). Their replies run the beat's own options (call:slot:N): 1 ask where
# it came from, 2 ask who it's for (two questions at most, counting what your hands turn over), then
# 3 take the trade, 4 refuse it, 5 the other way. What follows each is the beat's own line.

conv duty.swap.ring
for duty:swap:ring
topic "About the ring."
prio quest
voice haven

node start
  say It's a good ring. Gold, not plated. He bought it in the year we had the flood, when there was nothing, so you know he meant it.
  say Two tins. That's all. It's not for me, before you think it.
  > @where Is it yours to sell? -> more   do call:slot:1
  > @who Who are the tins for? -> more   do call:slot:2
  > @terms Let's settle it. -> terms

node more
  say He turns the empty finger with his thumb, round and round, where the ring used to sit.
  > @ask I've another question. -> start
  > @settle Let's settle it. -> terms

node terms
  say So. Two tins, or not.
  > @take Two tins for the ring. -> end   do call:slot:3
  > @no Keep your ring. I can't take it. -> end   do call:slot:4
  > @third Tins now. The ring, when you can. -> end   do call:slot:5

conv duty.swap.watch
for duty:swap:watch
topic "That's a man's watch."
prio quest
voice plain

node start
  say It goes. Listen. It ticks. You have to wind it in the morning or it stops, I know how, I do it every day.
  say Bread. A whole one, if you've got a whole one.
  > @where Where did you get it? -> more   do call:slot:1
  > @who Who's the bread for? -> more   do call:slot:2
  > @terms All right. Let's see. -> terms

node more
  say He holds the watch to his ear again while you think, as if it might have stopped since.
  > @ask Tell me something else. -> start
  > @settle All right. Let's see. -> terms

node terms
  say Is it a yes?
  > @take Bread for the watch. -> end   do call:slot:3
  > @no I can't take that watch. -> end   do call:slot:4
  > @third Bread. The watch goes in the book. -> end   do call:slot:5

conv duty.swap.coat
for duty:swap:coat
topic "Put your coat back on."
prio quest
voice haven

node start
  say It's warm enough in here. Feel it, it's a good coat, wool, not that army stuff. Lined at the pockets.
  say A tin of beef. That's a fair price for a coat that good. Anyone would say so.
  > @where Have you another coat? -> more   do call:slot:1
  > @who Who's the tin for? -> more   do call:slot:2
  > @terms Let's settle it. -> terms

node more
  say He stands very straight, the way a cold man does when he's decided not to shiver in front of you.
  > @ask Hold on. One more thing. -> start
  > @settle Let's settle it. -> terms

node terms
  say Well?
  > @take The tin for the coat. -> end   do call:slot:3
  > @no Keep the coat on. -> end   do call:slot:4
  > @third An hour at the woodpile for the tin. -> end   do call:slot:5

conv duty.swap.aspirin
for duty:swap:aspirin
topic "Let me see the packet."
prio quest
voice plain

node start
  say Antibiotics. Real ones, sealed, from the hospital before it went. You can't get these for love.
  say Six tins is a gift. I could get eight at the camp. I'd rather they went to a house.
  > @where Which hospital? Which shelf? -> more   do call:slot:1
  > @who Who are you selling for? -> more   do call:slot:2
  > @terms Let's settle it. -> terms

node more
  say He smiles the whole time. It's a very good smile. It doesn't change at all.
  > @ask I'm not finished asking. -> start
  > @settle Let's settle it. -> terms

node terms
  say Six tins. Final.
  > @take Six tins for the packet. -> end   do call:slot:3
  > @no No. Take it somewhere else. -> end   do call:slot:4
  > @third Let me call the nurse to look first. -> end   do call:slot:5

conv duty.swap.stolen
for duty:swap:stolen
topic "Where's the spoon from?"
prio quest
voice plain

node start
  say Solid silver, that. Look at the weight. One tin and it's yours, I'm not greedy.
  say Don't look over there. Look at the spoon.
  > @where Where did you find it? -> more   do call:slot:1
  > @who Who's the tin for? -> more   do call:slot:2
  > @terms Let's settle it. -> terms

node more
  say Across the room the old man has his hand over his signet ring, as if it might go next.
  > @ask Hang on. -> start
  > @settle Let's settle it. -> terms

node terms
  say One tin. Quick, before I change my mind.
  > @take A tin for the spoon. -> end   do call:slot:3
  > @no Put it away. -> end   do call:slot:4
  > @third Let's ask the gentleman whose spoon it is. -> end   do call:slot:5

conv duty.swap.hoard
for duty:swap:hoard
topic "That's every candle we have."
prio quest
voice haven

node start
  say And I'll pay for every one, fair price, more than fair. Look in the sack. Tins, good ones, no dents.
  say A man who plans ahead isn't a villain. He's just early.
  > @where Where did all the tins come from? -> more   do call:slot:1
  > @who Who are the candles for? -> more   do call:slot:2
  > @terms Let's settle it. -> terms

node more
  say He pats the sack, the way you'd pat a dog that's done well.
  > @ask One more question. -> start
  > @settle Let's settle it. -> terms

node terms
  say All of them. What do you say?
  > @take Every candle, for the tins. -> end   do call:slot:3
  > @no No. Not to you. -> end   do call:slot:4
  > @third Four, like anyone else. -> end   do call:slot:5

conv duty.swap.proxy
for duty:swap:proxy
topic "Let me read the list."
prio quest
voice haven

node start
  say Lamp oil, salt, and a needle, a proper one, for wool. Grandad says the eggs are worth more than that. Grandad says to say so.
  say I'm only fetching. It's not my list.
  > @where Why didn't your grandad come? -> more   do call:slot:1
  > @who Is any of it for you? -> more   do call:slot:2
  > @terms Let's see what we've got. -> terms

node more
  say His eyes go to the jar of boiled sweets at the end of the table, and away, and back.
  > @ask Wait, I've a question. -> start
  > @settle Let's see what we've got. -> terms

node terms
  say Can I have them? The things on the list?
  > @take The list, for the eggs. -> end   do call:slot:3
  > @no Your grandad has to come himself. -> end   do call:slot:4
  > @third The list for four eggs. Keep two. -> end   do call:slot:5

conv duty.swap.crew
for duty:swap:crew
topic "You're not from round here."
prio quest
voice redhand

node start
  say Good rounds, those. Clean, no misfires. I'm not here to make trouble. I'm here for dressings and whatever you've got for a fever.
  say I'll say it once. The rounds are a fair price, and I'm a polite customer.
  > @where Where's your camp? -> more   do call:slot:1
  > @who Who's hurt? -> more   do call:slot:2
  > @terms Let's settle it. -> terms

node more
  say His eyes go to the door, the window, the lookout's ladder, and back to you, as if he were reading a price list.
  > @ask I've something else to ask. -> start
  > @settle Let's settle it. -> terms

node terms
  say Yes or no.
  > @take Dressings for the rounds. -> end   do call:slot:3
  > @no Not for the Red Hand. -> end   do call:slot:4
  > @third A dressing for the lad. No rounds. -> end   do call:slot:5

conv duty.swap.cash
for duty:swap:cash
topic "That's a lot of money."
prio quest
voice plain

node start
  say It's all there. You can count it. I'd like you to count it, actually. It's been a while.
  say A loaf. I know what it looks like. I know what it's worth now. I'd still like it counted.
  > @where Where's this from? -> more   do call:slot:1
  > @who Who's the loaf for? -> more   do call:slot:2
  > @terms Let's settle it. -> terms

node more
  say He squares the edges of the notes with two fingers, the way he must have done it for years at a desk.
  > @ask One more thing. -> start
  > @settle Let's settle it. -> terms

node terms
  say A loaf, then?
  > @take A loaf for the notes. -> end   do call:slot:3
  > @no Keep your money. -> end   do call:slot:4
  > @third A loaf for an afternoon on the sums. -> end   do call:slot:5

conv duty.swap.pearls
for duty:swap:pearls
topic "Those are real."
prio quest
voice haven

node start
  say My mother wore them to her wedding and to his funeral and nowhere in between. Every one is knotted. If the string goes, you only lose one.
  say I want his name on the truck list. Pavel Roux. Fourteen. He's strong.
  > @where Are they yours to give? -> more   do call:slot:1
  > @who Is he here? -> more   do call:slot:2
  > @terms Let's talk about the list. -> terms

node more
  say He doesn't touch the pearls. He looks at the door, where a boy is pretending not to wait.
  > @ask I need to ask you something. -> start
  > @settle Let's talk about the list. -> terms

node terms
  say Will you put him on it?
  > @take I'll take the pearls. -> end   do call:slot:3
  > @no The list isn't for sale. -> end   do call:slot:4
  > @third Keep them. Come and see the clerk. -> end   do call:slot:5

conv duty.swap.papers
for duty:swap:papers
topic "What are these papers?"
prio quest
voice plain

node start
  say Travel papers. Stamped by the regional office, signed, the proper form. Show these at the line and you walk out.
  say Three sets. A week's food. That's a price for a life, isn't it?
  > @where Have you seen them work? -> more   do call:slot:1
  > @who Who are these for? -> more   do call:slot:2
  > @terms Let's settle it. -> terms

node more
  say He keeps one hand on the folder the whole time, as if the papers might believe him and walk off.
  > @ask Let me ask you something. -> start
  > @settle Let's settle it. -> terms

node terms
  say A week's food. Last offer.
  > @take A week's food for the papers. -> end   do call:slot:3
  > @no No. Go somewhere else. -> end   do call:slot:4
  > @third Lookout, come and see these. -> end   do call:slot:5

conv duty.swap.tools
for duty:swap:tools
topic "Those are good chisels."
prio quest
voice haven

node start
  say The best in the valley. My father's, then mine. I'm not selling them. I'm leaving them with you while my hands mend.
  say Two tins a week while they're on your shelf. I'll want every one back. I'll know if one's missing.
  > @where What happened to your hands? -> more   do call:slot:1
  > @who Who'll use them meanwhile? -> more   do call:slot:2
  > @terms Let's settle it. -> terms

node more
  say He unrolls the cloth a little, touches each handle in turn, and rolls it up again.
  > @ask One thing before we settle. -> start
  > @settle Let's settle it. -> terms

node terms
  say Will you keep them?
  > @take Two tins, and the tools are ours. -> end   do call:slot:3
  > @no We're not a pawnshop. -> end   do call:slot:4
  > @third On the shelf, for a week's work. -> end   do call:slot:5

conv duty.swap.boots
for duty:swap:boots
topic "Whose boots are those?"
prio quest
voice plain

node start
  say They're good boots. Leather. Our brother's, he doesn't need them. Two pairs of anything for one pair of these.
  say Anything. Clogs. Slippers. We're not fussy.
  > @where Where's your brother? -> more   do call:slot:1
  > @who Who are the pairs for? -> more   do call:slot:2
  > @terms Let's settle it. -> terms

node more
  say They stand on one foot each on the cold floor, and change feet, together, without noticing.
  > @ask Tell me something else. -> start
  > @settle Let's settle it. -> terms

node terms
  say Is it a deal?
  > @take The boots for two pairs of clogs. -> end   do call:slot:3
  > @no Where is he, really? -> end   do call:slot:4
  > @third Clogs. The boots stay, named. -> end   do call:slot:5

conv duty.swap.salt
for duty:swap:salt
topic "Salt, is it?"
prio quest
voice plain

node start
  say From the pans on the coast. A third of the sack for flour, weight for weight. You know what salt's worth with winter coming.
  > @where Which pans? Which coast? -> more   do call:slot:1
  > @who Who's the flour for? -> more   do call:slot:2
  > @terms Let's settle it. -> terms

node more
  say He keeps the sack tied at the bottom with his hand on the knot.
  > @ask Hold on. -> start
  > @settle Let's settle it. -> terms

node terms
  say Weight for weight?
  > @take Flour for the sack, weight for weight. -> end   do call:slot:3
  > @no No trade. -> end   do call:slot:4
  > @third Flour for the top half, weighed dry. -> end   do call:slot:5

conv duty.swap.letter
for duty:swap:letter
topic "Who's the letter to?"
prio quest
voice haven

node start
  say To my daughter, Vera. She's in Saint-Philippe, on the street by the mill. The tin's for whoever carries it. It's a good tin, peaches.
  say Somebody will be going north. Next week, perhaps.
  > @where How long have you been bringing it? -> more   do call:slot:1
  > @who When did you last hear from her? -> more   do call:slot:2
  > @terms Let's talk about it. -> terms

node more
  say He has the letter in both hands, the corners soft from being carried.
  > @ask I want to ask you something. -> start
  > @settle Let's talk about it. -> terms

node terms
  say Will you take it?
  > @take The letter and the tin, for the box. -> end   do call:slot:3
  > @no That street burned, Josef. -> end   do call:slot:4
  > @third The letter, not the tin. -> end   do call:slot:5

conv duty.swap.knife
for duty:swap:knife
topic "That's a sharp little knife."
prio quest
voice plain

node start
  say It's too small now. I've sharpened it down to nothing. I want a proper one. A bread knife, or a butcher's.
  say I'll trade this and a day's mending. I'm good at mending.
  > @where What do you need it for? -> more   do call:slot:1
  > @who Who's it for? -> more   do call:slot:2
  > @terms Let's settle it. -> terms

node more
  say He holds the little knife the way you hold a thing you've held for a long time, without looking at it.
  > @ask Tell me one more thing. -> start
  > @settle Let's settle it. -> terms

node terms
  say Will you swap?
  > @take A bigger knife for yours. -> end   do call:slot:3
  > @no No knives for you. -> end   do call:slot:4
  > @third Keep both. Go and see the lookout. -> end   do call:slot:5
